# =============================================================================
# Suite-level .gitignore
#
# Each pipeline owns its own .gitignore under pipelines/<name>/, because
# gitignore patterns containing a slash are anchored to the directory holding the
# file. Keeping pipeline rules beside the pipeline means moving a pipeline can
# never silently unignore its real configs — which is exactly what happened when
# the SV pipeline was first moved into pipelines/sv/.
#
# This file holds only:
#   1. cruft that can appear anywhere in the tree
#   2. a defensive net of SLASH-FREE patterns for files that must never be
#      committed regardless of depth
#
# A pattern without a slash matches at every level, so the rules below apply
# throughout the suite and survive any future reorganisation.
# =============================================================================

# --- Defensive net: real configs, at any depth -------------------------------
# These name real samples and absolute local paths. The negations keep the
# templates tracked. Slash-free, so they hold wherever a pipeline is moved to.
pipeline_config.yaml
pipeline_config_*.yaml
reference_paths.yaml
sample_sheet.tsv
sample_sheet_*.tsv
!pipeline_config.example.yaml
!reference_paths.example.yaml
!sample_sheet.example.tsv

# --- Patient / sequencing data, at any depth ---------------------------------
# Never commit these regardless of where they turn up. tests/fixtures/ is
# re-included by each pipeline's own .gitignore, which is evaluated later and
# therefore wins for those paths.
*.bam
*.bam.bai
*.cram
*.cram.crai
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bedmethyl
*.bedmethyl.gz
*.bedmethyl.gz.tbi
*.fa
*.fa.fai
*.fasta
*.gtf
*.gtf.gz

# --- Run manifests -----------------------------------------------------------
# Written to a results/ root, so a `results/*/*` style rule never catches them.
# They record real sample IDs, absolute paths and hostnames.
*.run_manifest.tsv

# --- Scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.swp
work/

# --- R -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# macOS AppleDouble metadata. The SSD this is developed on is not a native macOS
# filesystem, so every file written from macOS gets a ._ sibling.
._*
.AppleDouble
